Z||000010||Old Lar||12-27-2001||02:01 PM||||I'm 60 miles east of Buffalo and nary a flake, but if the wind shifts from from westerly breezes to southerly breezes, I'll get dumped on from Lake Ontario lake effect snow.  I'll have to haul out my snowthrower for sure.  Of course it was 17* F (-8C*) this morning too.  Hate the cold.||||reg||10
Z||000011||AkursedX||12-27-2001||02:13 PM||||Blah!  I give up.  I went out and shoveled again.  It was only about 7 inches of snow, not the 12 inches I said in my last post.  <P>Itstopped snowing so I figured I could get everything snow free, and move my cars around in the driveway to clean them off.<P>Well by the time I was cleaning off my mom's car, it started snowing again.  By the time I got in, which was about 20 minutes later, there was already 2-3 inches on the ground, and it's still coming.<P>I really have to pray that it stops soon.  I'm supposed to be going to visit my girlfriend in Pittsburg on saturday!!!  (I'm taking a greyhound, not my Fiero)  I hope everything gets plowed by then so I can leave!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||12-27-2001||05:17 PM||||I totally agree AkursedX!!  This is crazy!  I also cannot believe they didn't shut everything down this morning before everyone left for work.  By 10:30 they were closing the city down anyway, and it wasn't like this was a surprise.<P>We've got about 50 inches or so here (in Depew) so far since Christmas eve.  Here is a pic I took Christmas morning from inside of my garage showing the depth.  This is only about the first 25 inches.  The snow piles alongside our driveway are now taller than I am.  Its like the ice planet in Star Wars around here!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads\probesnow.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||AkursedX||12-27-2001||07:33 PM||||Well I see my city has made national news once again.  It was the 3rd story on ABC's nightly news!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Right now it has stopped snowing and I got all caught up, but it's supposed to start again in the evening and were supposed to get hit with at least another foot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  So I gotta get up at 5am so I can shovel enough to get my mothers car free so she can go to work.  <P>Fformula88:  That picture you took does not do this weather justice!  Like you said, there was about twice that on the ground this afternoon.||||reg||1
