Z||000017||Master_Sushi||12-28-2001||02:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I HATE this city!!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> I live in Lewiston not the Falls. I just put Niagara in my user info becuase everyone knows where that is. I hate my city also  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. But for allot of other reasons then snow! I won't go into them all now because I don't feel like bitching. I'm moving to ontario this spring/summer. Geting out of New York will be one of the better things I've ever done.<P>Oh and niagara area hasen't had much snow at all. The lake snow bands allwys just go a bit south of us. I can drive 5 mins at times and hit blizzard like conditions if I want. But when I drive back to where I live its clear sky all the way.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||AkursedX||12-28-2001||02:29 PM||||Here is my house at 12:00 last night.  I actually had a plow come down my street, so I shoveled out the entire driveway.  <P>By the time I was done, as you can tell, the snow began to fall again.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PC280016.JPG"> <P><BR>I would of taken a picture of it this morning, but the batteries in my camera had died, but there was 19 fresh inches of snow on the ground.  I have had to to sacrifice the walkways in front of my house to beable to clear my driveway because there is simply no other place to put it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Voytek||12-28-2001||02:30 PM||||-10*C (14*F) and snowing here right now.  We've had snow for Christmas - a few left over inches from a couple weeks back.  It's supposed to hit -25*C tonight (-13*F).  We're in for a cold, cold weekend.<P>Screwie - I know what you mean.  I'm not a fan of really cold weather but I would take a white cold winter any day over a rainy one.<P>WOW Akursed!!! That's a lot of snow!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>The last time I've seen this much snow here was about 4 years ago.  Have fun!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fformula88||12-28-2001||06:26 PM||||Thats a lot of snow, but not nearly as much as we have now.  I am going to take some pictures tomorrow and will try to post a couple.  I've got snow piles along my driveway that are about 8 feet high.  I am 6 foot and they are a lot higher than me.  The snow in the front lawn is up to the botton of my front window.  <P>So far about 83 inches have fallen, and there is 44 inches on the ground.  (The snow compacts as it piles up)  News reports say a lot of private plows (like on pickups) are breaking down from the strain of so much snow!  Someone was also killed when his carport roof collapsed on him while he was clearing his driveway.  This is a bit more snow than we really needed for a white Christmas!  ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Fformula88||12-28-2001||08:31 PM||||Here are a few up to the minute pics of what it looks like in my driveway, although they still do not do it justice.  Its like living in a cave since you really cannot see down the street anymore the snow is so high.<P>My 97 Probe daily driver.  Snow behind it is high, and the driveway is sloping down towards the street.  Out at the street the snowpile stands about 7 foot high (or higher).  I am 6 foot and its a lot higher than I stand!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/probesnow2.JPG"> <P><BR>My daily driver again... with ugly hubcaps on my winter wheels.  This isn't the highest snowpile around, but its still higher than the roof of the car!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/probesnow3.JPG"> <P><BR>The big snow pile is my mothers car.  The car under the cover in the garage is my Fiero staying nice and toasty warm for the winter.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/probesnow4.JPG"> <P><BR>This is looking at the snow hill across the street from me.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/probesnow5.JPG"> <P>So who wants to move to Buffalo?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  They can have my house!!<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
